  "id": "mlops-loop",
  "after": "overview",
  "title": "The MLOps loop, tool by tool.",
  "caption": "Each step has one job and a common free tool, and each matches a part of the cloud kitchen. The green arrow on the left makes it a loop. When monitoring (निगरानी, nigrani) shows that live data has changed, you collect new data and retrain. The new model then goes through the same tests and packing again.",
  "alt": "Seven numbered steps in three groups. Build: version data with DVC (dated ingredient batches), track runs with MLflow (the recipe register), serve the model with FastAPI or Gradio (the order window). Ship: test changes with GitHub Actions, package with Docker (the sealed box), go live on Render or Hugging Face Spaces. Watch: monitor with logs and drift checks (regular tasting). An arrow labelled new data, retrain loops from step 7 back to step 1.",
